QIDI Box source lineage (GPLv3)
-------------------------------

The QIDI Box Klipper modules originate in QIDI's GPLv3 fork of Klipper
(https://github.com/QIDITECH/klipper, branch PLUS4). QIDI shipped them as open
Python source through firmware 1.7.0 and as compiled Cython .so from 1.7.1.

QIDI's authoritative 1.7.0 source is preserved at
analysis/github-releases/qidi-klipper-1.7.0-box-source/ (GPLv3).

A community snapshot of these files (analysis/components/lineage-source/ is
derived from it, and its LICENSE.published-baseline records it) is often cited
as MIT-licensed by stew675. That snapshot is byte-identical to QIDI's GPLv3
1.7.0 source; because it is QIDI's GPLv3 code, the MIT label does not govern it
— GPLv3 code cannot be relicensed to MIT by a third party. Treat all of this
Box source, and anything built from it, as GPLv3. The MIT text is retained only
as a record of how that snapshot was published, not as the operative license.


Rebuilt QIDI Box modules (qidibox-modules/, GPLv3)
--------------------------------------------------

qidibox-modules/ contains compiled Klipper extension binaries (.so) for the
QIDI Box, produced for CPython 3.12 and CPython 3.7 on aarch64. They are a
clean compile of QIDI's GPLv3 Box source described above (see
qidibox-modules/build-recipe/SOURCE-MANIFEST.txt for exact inputs and build
environments).

These are NOT QIDI's proprietary firmware binaries; no QIDI compiled component
is redistributed — they are built from source. Because the source is GPLv3, the
binaries are GPLv3 (qidibox-modules/LICENSE is the GPLv3). The corresponding
source is available both upstream and in this repository at the path above, and
the build recipe is in qidibox-modules/build-recipe/, satisfying the GPL's
source-availability requirement for distributed binaries.


